hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"228","Idha sami'tum sayaha ad-diyakah fa'salu Allaha min fadlihi, fa-innaha ra'at malakan, wa idha sami'tum nahiqa al-himari fa'ta'widhu billahi min ash-shaytani, fa-innahu ra'a shaytanan.. When you hear the crowing of a rooster, ask Allah for His grace, for it has seen an angel. And when you hear the braying of a donkey, seek refuge in Allah from Satan, for it has seen a devil."
"229","Idha sami'tum nubāha al-kilābi wa nahīqa al-ḥamīri bi-l-layli fa-ta'awwidhū bi-Llāhi minhunna; fa-innahunna yarayna mā tarawn.. When you hear the barking of dogs and the braying of donkeys at night, seek refuge in Allah from them, for they see what you do not see."
